# playpick cell: mode=clear spec=shaman:elemental style=flee size=10
# difficulty=normal view=390x844,touch save=fresh.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl first (grepped every shaman:elemental line and every
# mode=clear line): shaman:elemental has two prior clear-mode evenings, both
# 25-heroic on a carried save (good, then melee) -- never flee, and never at
# this spec's own default 10-normal/fresh tier. flee itself has run through
# mode=clear/walk many times (direction.md's #3, thirteen confirmations) but
# never paired with this class. This is also the first fresh-save touch clear
# evening (390x844) for shaman:elemental at all.
#
# Also worth watching for, from a source read this session did while the gate
# was shut (src/main.ts): harvest() (~line 1039) only fires while
# state.mode==='travel', and walkTo() (~line 1274) calls harvest() before
# resetting roomCarried from run.carried -- so a corridor retry re-harvests
# the still-dead state's shares (all -1) into run.carried an instant after
# restart()'s own wipedRoom() reset, and carryInto() (~line 859) then paints
# those dead shares onto the freshly built corridor actors. That would explain
# #271's hp=0/locked-on-arrival shape without needing a pad ride at all. Not
# something this session can fully confirm by playing -- it is a reading of
# the code, not a measurement -- but if this cell wipes in a corridor, this is
# what to look at in the journal: does run.carried go negative between
# wipedRoom() and the retry's first tick.
open
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:shaman:elemental
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start
targets
ui
evening flee 240 10
